(Shen Yanlin)

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,940
♪Cruel world, where trust runs thin♪
(Ling Che)

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,320
♪Blades clash. Who will rise above?♪
(Shuangdao Hui)

5
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:28,040
♪Behind every smile, danger waits♪
(Dongshan Tai)

6
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,520
(Fei Liu)

7
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:35,080
♪Know your limits, know your worth♪
(Luo Song)

8
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,800
♪Stand strong against the raging tide♪
(Annie)

9
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:44,120
♪Ask how many times I've lost my way♪

10
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:49,000
♪Storms rage on the road to power♪

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,960
♪Let old promises fade into memory♪

12
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:58,040
♪Alone and fearless, I won't back down♪

13
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:02,120
♪Power is a crown forged in blood♪

14
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:09,040
♪Brotherhood is shelter from the storm♪

15
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,680
=The Underworld=

16
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,520
Fu.

17
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,079
Can I put the candles here?

18
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:19,640
Sure.

19
00:01:22,879 --> 00:01:24,040
Boss Che, you're here.

20
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:25,640
Che.

21
00:01:26,159 --> 00:01:27,200
You're here.

22
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:27,640
Fu.

23
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:28,799
Happy birthday.

24
00:01:29,519 --> 00:01:31,120
Thanks.

25
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:31,920
Boss Che.

26
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:33,439
My brother's birthday is August 6.

27
00:01:33,799 --> 00:01:34,840
Mine's June 8.

28
00:01:34,959 --> 00:01:35,640
What are the odds?

29
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,799
When's your birthday?

30
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:39,560
Today.

31
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:43,760
Perfect. Let's celebrate together.

32
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:45,280
I don't celebrate birthdays.

33
00:01:46,319 --> 00:01:47,079
You will today.

34
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:48,920
Che

35
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:54,560
is Lin's brother too.

36
00:01:57,879 --> 00:01:59,159
Come on. Celebrate with us.

37
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,079
Boss Che, make a wish.

38
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,799
Okay.

39
00:02:07,719 --> 00:02:10,439
♪Happy birthday to you♪

40
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,120
♪Happy birthday to you♪

41
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:17,439
♪Happy birthday to you♪

42
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,680
Bad Che!

43
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,680
Bad Che! Bad Che!

44
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:27,840
Blow out the candles.

45
00:02:30,439 --> 00:02:31,919
Three, two, one.

46
00:02:33,639 --> 00:02:34,360
Happy birthday!

47
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:37,599
Fu.

48
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,439
Let's cut the cake.

49
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:41,280
I'll do it.

50
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:43,120
Why do you always have that huge knife?

51
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:45,879
You need a knife to cut cake, right?

52
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:47,800
Give Fu the biggest piece.

53
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,400
Right.

54
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:49,560
Fu gets the biggest.

55
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:52,879
Here, Boss Che.

56
00:02:56,879 --> 00:02:57,599
This one's mine.

57
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:58,800
What about mine?

58
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,840
The rest is yours.

59
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:02,759
Here, Fu. Eat up.

60
00:03:02,799 --> 00:03:05,264
♪Open your arms♪

61
00:03:05,838 --> 00:03:08,897
♪Embrace every pain you can't endure♪

62
00:03:09,379 --> 00:03:12,548
♪Let love's warmth turn into a rainbow♪

63
00:03:12,548 --> 00:03:15,458
♪And light up our sky♪

64
00:03:16,107 --> 00:03:18,721
♪Open your arms♪

65
00:03:18,999 --> 00:03:22,113
♪Embrace all the pain♪

66
00:03:22,632 --> 00:03:25,690
♪Let love's warmth turn into a rainbow♪

67
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:29,138
♪And light up our sky♪

68
00:03:29,379 --> 00:03:32,363
♪Look up♪

69
00:03:32,363 --> 00:03:35,903
♪Gaze into the endless night♪

70
00:03:35,959 --> 00:03:40,000
♪Believe a shooting star will streak by♪

71
00:03:40,278 --> 00:03:42,650
♪And light up your dreams♪

72
00:03:42,798 --> 00:03:45,319
♪Open your arms♪

73
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:48,860
♪Embrace all the pain♪

74
00:03:49,101 --> 00:03:52,011
♪Let love's warmth turn into a rainbow♪

75
00:03:52,252 --> 00:03:54,198
♪And light up our sky♪

76
00:03:54,199 --> 00:03:55,120
Quick, quick!

77
00:03:55,319 --> 00:03:56,000
Come on, come on!

78
00:03:56,599 --> 00:03:58,080
Three, two, one.

79
00:04:02,057 --> 00:04:04,281
♪Our sky♪

80
00:04:05,671 --> 00:04:08,897
=Episode 10=

81
00:04:08,897 --> 00:04:10,900
(1999)

82
00:04:13,919 --> 00:04:14,599
Boss.

83
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,879
There are only a few of us.

84
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,519
Why'd you order so much food?

85
00:04:17,639 --> 00:04:18,519
Are your friends coming?

86
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,759
Can we even finish all this?

87
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,879
You wouldn't understand.

88
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,240
My brother and I used to

89
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:27,279
fight just to get something to eat.

90
00:04:28,079 --> 00:04:30,920
Now I can eat whatever I want

91
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,680
and buy my brother whatever he wants.

92
00:04:37,879 --> 00:04:38,720
Unlike you.

93
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:39,759
You've never gone hungry.

94
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:44,959
Wangcai.

95
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,639
What do you want to eat?

96
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:50,600
Hey.

97
00:04:52,079 --> 00:04:53,839
I went hungry with you too, you know.

98
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,600
Ling Che.

99
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:03,399
Even if my own dad showed up today,

100
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,639
he couldn't save you.

101
00:05:05,399 --> 00:05:05,920
Kill him!

102
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,959
Why'd you come over here?

103
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,879
To save you, of course.

104
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,480
Thanks a lot.

105
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:37,040
Thanks.

106
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,120
Could you not hit my face?

107
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,399
Sure.

108
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:46,680
Sweetie.

109
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,879
Be good like me and you'll get fed.

110
00:05:52,839 --> 00:05:53,439
As for you...

111
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,800
What are you looking at?

112
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,439
Get lost.

113
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,240
Eat up, sweetie.

114
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,839
What's wrong with you?

115
00:06:13,839 --> 00:06:14,519
Stop eating.

116
00:06:14,959 --> 00:06:16,079
S-Share some with me.

117
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:19,959
What did I teach you?

118
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,439
Bro, we haven't eaten in three days.

119
00:06:22,759 --> 00:06:23,879
Let's eat first.

120
00:06:25,879 --> 00:06:26,920
If you hadn't rushed over,

121
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,160
we wouldn't be tied up here,

122
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,839
eating this dog food.

123
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:31,959
Only dogs eat this stuff.

124
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:33,920
If there were meat, would you eat it?

125
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,240
No.

126
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:37,839
Stop blaming yourself.

127
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,360
I don't regret saving you.

128
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,199
Save me some.

129
00:06:44,759 --> 00:06:45,600
Save me some.

130
00:06:49,959 --> 00:06:51,680
I asked. You said you didn't want any.

131
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,639
Get lower.

132
00:07:05,639 --> 00:07:06,519
This is so good.

133
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,720
Save the meat for me.

134
00:07:11,839 --> 00:07:12,560
Thanks, buddy.

135
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,560
Remember now?

136
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:23,639
Fu.

137
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:25,519
What else do you want?

138
00:07:25,639 --> 00:07:26,319
Goose.

139
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,279
I want to eat goose.

140
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:31,319
Coming right up.

141
00:07:33,959 --> 00:07:34,439
Eat.

142
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,279
Che, pull it apart for me.

143
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,079
Hold on.

144
00:07:51,639 --> 00:07:52,959
From now on,

145
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,360
they're not just geese anymore.

146
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,839
They're our golden geese.

147
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:01,240
Over there.

148
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,399
You want to hide the goods

149
00:08:10,959 --> 00:08:12,600
inside the geese?

150
00:08:15,279 --> 00:08:16,560
The new place needs to make money.

151
00:08:16,959 --> 00:08:18,680
Any ideas for the slot machines?

152
00:08:19,079 --> 00:08:20,240
Hutou Jun made good money

153
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,800
off slot machines over the years.

154
00:08:22,439 --> 00:08:24,079
But compared to these jewels,

155
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,079
that's nothing.

156
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:28,560
When Boss Hui was in the jewelry trade,

157
00:08:29,439 --> 00:08:31,560
he built connections with gem mines

158
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,200
in several neighboring countries.

159
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,080
The costs are low.

160
00:08:33,519 --> 00:08:36,519
A little processing, and profits soar.

161
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:38,879
That keeps Boss Hui's cash flow steady.

162
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,039
As for the slot machines,

163
00:08:41,639 --> 00:08:42,559
once the cops back off,

164
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:44,200
we can bring them in later.

165
00:08:44,399 --> 00:08:47,480
Using geese to smuggle jewelry

166
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,879
is pretty clever.

167
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,720
The cops won't catch on easily.

168
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,519
But the old route is too risky.

169
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,679
The shantytown isn't far from here.

170
00:08:57,639 --> 00:08:59,919
My brother and I grew up there.

171
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,240
I could find my way around blindfolded.

172
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,519
Plus, in the shantytown,

173
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,879
fights and robberies are common.

174
00:09:08,399 --> 00:09:09,639
The cops are understaffed,

175
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,600
and the border checkpoints are lax.

176
00:09:13,919 --> 00:09:16,000
I'll tell our guys in nearby countries

177
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:17,720
to start a goose farm too.

178
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,279
Have a drink, Boss Hui.

179
00:09:22,639 --> 00:09:23,879
Boss Hui, your shoulders are so tense.

180
00:09:25,159 --> 00:09:26,080
Spit it out.

181
00:09:27,399 --> 00:09:28,720
The plan is perfect,

182
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,440
except for one thing.

183
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,720
Transporting live poultry

184
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:35,120
requires a quarantine certificate.

185
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,919
You can handle that, Boss Hui.

186
00:09:37,279 --> 00:09:38,279
Stop this. I'm good.

187
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,720
Now I have to handle the permits too?

188
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,120
Boss Hui.

189
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,559
They're strict about this right now.

190
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:47,720
You need a guarantor company

191
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,519
and proof of livestock farming.

192
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,120
The whole process

193
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,279
takes at least two months.

194
00:09:52,279 --> 00:09:53,320
With your connections, it'll go faster.

195
00:09:55,159 --> 00:09:55,639
(Dongcheng Tiger)
Hold it.

196
00:09:56,519 --> 00:09:57,279
Well,

197
00:09:58,039 --> 00:09:58,879
Men Datou

198
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,120
has a nephew

199
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,279
named Hua or something.

200
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,120
He works at the Livestock Bureau.

201
00:10:05,759 --> 00:10:06,480
He could help.

202
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:08,840
That could work.

203
00:10:11,039 --> 00:10:12,080
Then we're set.

204
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:13,440
See? I told you.

205
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,399
With such a great boss,

206
00:10:14,399 --> 00:10:15,639
how could we not be great?

207
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,799
That's what I was gonna say.

208
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,519
Then we're set.

209
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:31,159
Boss Hui, with all your businesses,

210
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:32,720
why bother

211
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:34,440
with a little farm like mine?

212
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,399
I've made it this far

213
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,440
because my brothers had my back.

214
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:41,879
The cops are cracking down lately.

215
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:44,000
More help means more options.

216
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,639
As for the farm,

217
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:47,840
we'll split the profits

218
00:10:48,279 --> 00:10:49,120
between us.

219
00:10:51,279 --> 00:10:52,120
Actually,

220
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,639
I'd like to help you out, Boss Hui.

221
00:10:55,919 --> 00:10:56,840
But...

222
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:58,240
That nephew of his

223
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,200
is all talk.

224
00:11:00,919 --> 00:11:02,480
He doesn't have any connections.

225
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,120
So

226
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,799
I'm afraid I can't help.

227
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,639
Well, Boss Hui,

228
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:12,879
we'll get going.

229
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:27,519
Mr. Men.

230
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:37,519
Let's go.

231
00:11:41,399 --> 00:11:42,039
Boss Hui.

232
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,240
No luck?

233
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:55,039
Drink.

234
00:12:00,399 --> 00:12:01,320
Please let me.

235
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,519
Boss.

236
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:06,320
Men Datou's place barely makes money.

237
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,759
He only gets by

238
00:12:09,159 --> 00:12:11,320
taking a cut for doing favors.

239
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,600
What's with his wife's outfit today?

240
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,279
That jewelry set she's wearing,

241
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,879
I saw it at an auction.

242
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,000
It was insanely expensive.

243
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:22,279
How do you know I haven't seen it?

244
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,159
You know,

245
00:12:24,279 --> 00:12:26,519
he flaunts every cent he has.

246
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:28,600
What's odd about a jewelry set?

247
00:12:28,879 --> 00:12:29,399
No.

248
00:12:29,879 --> 00:12:32,519
Mr. Men didn't buy that jewelry.

249
00:12:33,159 --> 00:12:34,080
Dongshan Tai did.

250
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,000
I know how to win Mr. Men over.

251
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:43,720
But we'll need

252
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,720
one person.

253
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,159
Me?

254
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,879
Would you like to try it on?

255
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:05,120
Let me see that one.

256
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:05,840
Of course.

257
00:13:17,679 --> 00:13:19,639
Look. It suits you perfectly.

258
00:13:23,919 --> 00:13:26,639
Have you had this necklace appraised?

259
00:13:27,799 --> 00:13:28,679
What do you mean?

260
00:13:28,879 --> 00:13:31,720
Natural pearls usually have flaws.

261
00:13:32,519 --> 00:13:33,879
But this necklace

262
00:13:34,679 --> 00:13:36,080
looks almost too perfect.

263
00:13:37,039 --> 00:13:38,120
Take a look with this.

264
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:39,519
See if there's any whitish marks.

265
00:13:44,039 --> 00:13:44,919
This kind of spray coating

266
00:13:44,919 --> 00:13:46,879
is a common way to fake pearls.

267
00:13:47,279 --> 00:13:48,759
My husband paid a fortune for this!

268
00:13:48,759 --> 00:13:49,879
It cost him two...

269
00:13:53,759 --> 00:13:54,919
Two whole businesses?

270
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,279
Who are you?

271
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,559
Who I am doesn't matter.

272
00:14:00,879 --> 00:14:03,840
I'm not trying to embarrass you.

273
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,679
What are you getting at?

274
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,039
I'm just saying

275
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,200
whoever gave your husband that jewelry

276
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,480
couldn't even spring for decent coating.

277
00:14:20,039 --> 00:14:21,120
It's all taken care of.

278
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,200
Money.

279
00:14:33,919 --> 00:14:35,080
Come on. Be a man. Pay up.

280
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:35,879
Get lost.

281
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:45,279
I bought the clothes and shoes for that.

282
00:14:50,039 --> 00:14:50,639
You pay.

283
00:14:53,159 --> 00:14:53,799
Why?

284
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,639
It was your idea.

285
00:14:55,639 --> 00:14:56,759
Shouldn't you pay?

286
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,360
Come on. Be a man. Pay up.

287
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,519
Hey.

288
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:10,879
Thanks, bosses.

289
00:15:17,919 --> 00:15:19,080
What's wrong?

290
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:30,200
How'd you know

291
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:32,399
that would work on Men Datou's wife?

292
00:15:32,759 --> 00:15:34,559
Men Datou cares about appearances.

293
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:37,759
We embarrassed him in front of his wife.

294
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:40,039
That'll drive a wedge
between Dongshan Tai and him.

295
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,600
Then he might help Boss Hui

296
00:15:42,799 --> 00:15:43,759
take Dongshan Tai down.

297
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,159
Good thing you're my brother.

298
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,919
If you were my enemy,

299
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,360
you'd be a nightmare.

300
00:15:54,919 --> 00:15:57,080
What if I really were your enemy?

301
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,919
I'd just drop dead.

302
00:16:12,679 --> 00:16:13,519
Doesn't your hand hurt?

303
00:16:14,958 --> 00:16:18,702
♪You treated my true love like a game♪

304
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,890
♪Turns out your sweet words were empty♪

305
00:16:22,057 --> 00:16:25,264
♪Once you won, you walked away♪

306
00:16:26,042 --> 00:16:29,026
♪You took my true love with your lies♪

307
00:16:30,139 --> 00:16:33,105
♪My tears fall as I let you go♪

308
00:16:33,271 --> 00:16:36,201
♪You heartless man, would you dare♪

309
00:16:36,201 --> 00:16:40,778
♪Break the vows you swore to heaven♪

310
00:16:41,853 --> 00:16:45,152
♪I ask you, I ask you♪

311
00:16:45,783 --> 00:16:49,379
♪Do you have a conscience at all♪

312
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:55,829
♪I ask you, I ask you♪

313
00:16:56,459 --> 00:17:01,723
♪Were all your vows just lies♪

314
00:17:02,391 --> 00:17:05,152
♪I lost my youth and won loneliness♪

315
00:17:05,931 --> 00:17:08,359
♪Only then did I learn heartbreak♪

316
00:17:09,564 --> 00:17:12,270
♪I gave true love and got lies♪

317
00:17:12,974 --> 00:17:15,495
♪Now I see you for who you are♪

318
00:17:16,144 --> 00:17:19,036
♪From now on, I won't long for you♪

319
00:17:19,592 --> 00:17:22,798
♪Roses have thorns, so let them go♪

320
00:17:23,392 --> 00:17:26,858
♪I'll walk out of this storm♪

321
00:17:27,488 --> 00:17:32,085
♪I have to be brave♪

322
00:17:33,772 --> 00:17:37,330
♪I ask you, I ask you♪

323
00:17:37,738 --> 00:17:41,131
♪Do you have a conscience at all♪

324
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:47,560
♪I ask you, I ask you♪
